<p>The best writer on the smart home beat today is The Verge&#8217;s Jennifer Pattison Tuohy, who I think has the <a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1011431/apple-homeview-smart-display-best-feature?view_token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpZCI6ImdOQ1JwUVlyaEUiLCJwIjoiL3RlY2gvMTAxMTQzMS9hcHBsZS1ob21ldmlldy1zbWFydC1kaXNwbGF5LWJlc3QtZmVhdHVyZSIsImV4cCI6MTc5MjQ1NDM2MywiaWF0IjoxNzkyMDIyMzY0fQ.QIrWLDortJzKmvpZjNo9vJ_7caus1BpxgDnBr6JcHYA&#038;utm_medium=gift-link">best take on the HomeView I&#8217;ve seen so far</a>:</p>
<blockquote><p>
  HomeView’s simplicity may put off hardcore home automation enthusiasts, but I’d argue it’s perfect for their long-suffering spouses. I’ve tried every version of physical smart home control interface in my home, and you know who hasn’t used any of them? My family.</p>
<p>  Because my family all have iPhones, and because the HomeView will always be there and will feel familiar, I can see them actually using it. That means I could set up a <a href="https://www.theverge.com/report/869318/claude-vibe-coding-home-assistant-smart-home">full Home Assistant instance</a> and run a detailed dashboard on a tablet in my office, then feed <a href="https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/homekit/">the scenes and devices into Apple Home</a> so my husband and daughter can just tap to control them on a HomeView in the kitchen.</p>
<p>  HomeView may not be the <a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/993892/apples-next-computer-smart-home-hub-airport-router">smart home computer I want Apple to make</a>, but it is the smart home device Apple needed to make.
</p></blockquote>
<p>My own thermostat, which came with my HVAC system, is a piece of junk, and I can&#8217;t replace it because it is incompatible with third-party thermostats. But I can envision putting a HomeView on the wall and making that the primary interface for it and every other smart home device in my house.</p>
